Negative narrowing boundary, TARGET=unsigned char, same compiler command at
both -O0 and -O2; input has only parameter V v and adds VALUE:
VALUE             -256 -129 -128 -1L 255 256
GCC/Clang status  0/1  0/1  0/0  0/0 0/0 1/1
The three conflicting forms (unsigned variable to equal-width signed lane,
255 to signed-char lane, and negatives below signed lane minimum to an
unsigned lane) remain E2102, not an implicit selection of either oracle.

